@dtech77pl You were right — **Darcula was missing** from the theme dropdown!

**Root cause:** The theme engine loads `.vstheme` files and creates internal "NG" variants (`darculaNG`, `vs2015darkNG`, etc.) as base templates. Then it creates user-friendly embedded themes (`vs2015Light`, `vs2015Dark`, `vs2015Blue`) — but it was **not doing this for Darcula**. So the only dark theme with "darcula" in the name was the internal `darculaNG`, which was confusing and not what users expect.

